p @iobroker/testing 5.3.0 -> 6.1.0 (Issue #127, S0064)\n\nVerified both documented breaking changes are non-issues for this repo:\n- 6.0.0 dropped Node 18/20 support - we already require >=22 (package.json\n  engines, CI matrix tests 22.x/24.x/26.x only).\n- 6.1.0 changed harness.changeAdapterConfig() to auto-encrypt native fields\n  listed in encryptedNative - inspected the library''s own default\n  integration-test bootstrap (tests/integration/index.js in both the 5.3.0\n  and 6.1.0 tarballs): it only ever calls changeAdapterConfig with a\n  { common: {...} } payload, never native, so encryptNativeChanges()\n  short-circuits (empty field list) regardless of version. Our test files\n  (test/integration.js, test/package.js) use the zero-argument default API\n  and never call changeAdapterConfig themselves, so this change has no\n  effect here even though io-package.json does define encryptedNative:\n  [\"password\"].\n\nUndocumented but real transitive risk checked empirically: the bump also\npulls mocha ^11.7.6 -> ^12.0.0 (our own npm test invokes the hoisted mocha\nbinary directly, not just testing''s internal copy). Ran the full suite after\nthe bump: all 36 of our own tests (test:js) pass unchanged under mocha 12,\nand test:package now runs 50 checks (was 46) purely because the newer\ntesting package added checks (io-package.json/jsonConfig schema\nvalidation) - no removed or failing checks.","tree":{"sha":"19c28752a45ac2fa72b02ee13f5c414117a4f183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/19c28752a45ac2fa72b02ee13f5c414117a4f183"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/53086d4d58480b07ad8330d88ea4546aa23af416","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/53086d4d58480b07ad8330d88ea4546aa23af416","node_id":"C_kwDOMGdLNtoAKDUzMDg2ZDRkNTg0ODBiMDdhZDgzMzBkODhlYTQ1NDZhYTIzYWY0MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573","sha":"63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573"}],"sha":"53086d4d58480b07ad8330d88ea4546aa23af416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/53086d4d58480b07ad8330d88ea4546aa23af416"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:58:44Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:58:44Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"message":"release: v0.4.12 - Fix Issue #138: three robustness/functionality fixes for map handling on newer models with AES-encrypted map payloads (r2253c/w and similar). 1) A silent crash in the room-name fallback path (main.js): when the map file request failed, an unhandled TypeError showed up only as a generic error; now an early return with a clear debug message. 2) A model without an AES-IV table entry can never load its base map — this is now a persistent, recognizable condition (unsupportedMapModel) instead of the generic please-restart-the-adapter hint. 3) The old_map_data (piid 13) property, pushed specifically during active cleaning, could carry the same object_name-plus-AES-key format as the already-working piid 3 path, but was previously only logged as unimplemented and discarded; it now reuses the existing, already-verified decrypt pipeline (confirmed against the Home Assistant reference implementation), with a Debug-level log that masks the key material so it is safe to share in a public issue. Thanks to @luckyheiko for the detailed reports that made all three fixes possible.","tree":{"sha":"244b3e8e740d58f7bf4249911ff3ddf153134268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/244b3e8e740d58f7bf4249911ff3ddf153134268"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573","node_id":"C_kwDOMGdLNtoAKDYzZTRiNWYyYmRkN2RlZjk4ZTA0ZDFkOGYxODQ2YWVmMDk5ZGE1NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c","sha":"c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c"}],"sha":"63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/63e4b5f2bdd7def98e04d1d8f1846aef099da573"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:57:55Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:57:55Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"message":"Merge branch ''fix/issue-138-map-error-handling'' into main","tree":{"sha":"255cf375bd383a024680e8db0a9eddcf9cab2abc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/255cf375bd383a024680e8db0a9eddcf9cab2abc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c","node_id":"C_kwDOMGdLNtoAKGMyZTc4MjQ1MmYxYjdmNjM5NjRjN2RlMzI1ZTA4NTRjN2UwYzQzOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc","sha":"de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a","sha":"8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a"}],"sha":"c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c2e782452f1b7f63964c7de325e0854c7e0c438c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:50:54Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:53:46Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"message":"fix(map): decrypt old_map_data (piid 13) AES-map objects via existing pipeline (Issue #138)\n\nThe piid-13 (old_map_data) branch of _holeFrischeKarte(), which fires specifically\nduring active cleaning (P-frame pushes), only warned \"Entschluesselung nicht\nimplementiert\" for the 3-part \"<flag>,<object_name>,<aes_key>\" format and never\nattempted a download. Confirmed against the HA reference (Tasshack/dreame-vacuum,\nmap.py _request_i_map): it reconstructs the same \"<object_name>,<key>\" string used\nby the already-verified piid-3 path and feeds it through the identical decrypt\npipeline. No new crypto logic needed - just reassemble values[1]+'',''+values[2] into\nfreshObj so it flows through the existing comma-truncation-retry + AES-decrypt code\nunchanged. The piid-3-wins guard (else if (!freshObj)) is untouched.\n\nDebug-logs flag/object_name plus a truncated key_suffix (first 4 chars + length only,\nnot warn, to avoid log spam from frequent P-frame pushes during cleaning) so a real\npayload sample can be checked against this assumption if it turns out to differ for a\ngiven user - the key itself is masked since users will be asked to paste this exact\nline into the public GitHub issue.","tree":{"sha":"2bacbf1b2573e05d6fac0065ff4b48107781a798","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/2bacbf1b2573e05d6fac0065ff4b48107781a798"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a","node_id":"C_kwDOMGdLNtoAKDhmNDI0NzMzN2I0ZTRkZjNlMWZhMDRjMWE4ZjFhYzJiOTk0Y2ZkM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/7e137abdb9a83fa677a9340a856de148d23d0b86","sha":"7e137abdb9a83fa677a9340a856de148d23d0b86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/7e137abdb9a83fa677a9340a856de148d23d0b86"}],"sha":"8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/8f4247337b4e4df3e1fa04c1a8f1ac2b994cfd3a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:30:35Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:30:35Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"message":"release: v0.4.11 - Fix Issue #119: sync REMAP''d common metadata (name, states) to existing state objects at adapter start. In v0.4.8 the REMAP change for SIID 4/PIID 6 was correctly written to the in-memory spec but not to the persisted ioBroker objects, because _lazyCreateState only updates common.states when the cloud sends a get_properties response for that property — which may never happen for infrequently-changing properties. The frischwasser widget''s mop-pad-presence detection then fell back to the pulse-only source and displayed permanent not-installed even on REMAP''d devices. A new one-time-per-device migration (_syncRemapObjectMetadata, marker <did>.info.remapMetaSyncV2) now rebuilds the state objects with the correct metadata at adapter start. Thanks to @SilentM1978 for the diagnostic widget test that isolated the root cause to metadata persistence rather than the REMAP logic itself.","tree":{"sha":"4c6be3a7f72ea6a13e3bfe7b9fbf618fc5834e27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/4c6be3a7f72ea6a13e3bfe7b9fbf618fc5834e27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc","node_id":"C_kwDOMGdLNtoAKGRlNjljMzRlYzRjZTAwMjE5Y2IxNmY3MWU0NmU3NWNjZGI2MmE2ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998","sha":"c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998"}],"sha":"de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/de69c34ec4ce00219cb16f71e46e75ccdb62a6fc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T18:35:02Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T18:35:02Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"message":"fix(main): sync REMAP''d common metadata to existing state objects at adapter start\n\n_lazyCreateState only updates common when the cloud sends a\nget_properties response for the corresponding PIID. For infrequently-\nchanging properties like SIID 4/PIID 6 (water-tank / mop-pad presence\nvia REMAP) this may never happen in practice, so REMAP-changed states\nremain stuck with pre-REMAP metadata (e.g. old 3-value states-map with\nstale \"10\" key instead of the 2-value one). The frischwasser widget''s\n_waterTankIsRemapped detection then reads the stale states-map and\nfalls back to the pulse-only source, producing permanent \"not\ninstalled\" display even on properly REMAP''d devices.\n\nAdd _syncRemapObjectMetadata: a one-time per-device migration that\nsyncs common (name, states, type, role, unit) from specMetaDict at\nadapter start. Uses setObjectAsync with a fresh states-map to\ncleanly replace the field, rather than extendObjectAsync which\nrecursively merges and keeps stale keys.\n\nGuards:\n- Skip properties whose state object does not exist (Cloud never\n  sent a get_properties response for it yet).\n- Skip non-state objects (channels, devices) since setObjectAsync\n  would otherwise reject them for missing required fields.\n\nMarker <did>.info.remapMetaSyncV2 gates the migration to a single\nrun per device per marker version. V1 marker from an earlier\n(buggy) version of this migration is retained but ignored — the\nV2 pass runs regardless and correctly rebuilds affected\nstates-maps.\n\nConfirmed by @SilentM1978''s local widget-modification test on\nv0.4.10 (issue #119): a direct read of status.water-tank produced\ncorrect display and live updates on his r6001a, proving the adapter\nvalue and widget logic are right, and it''s the common.states\npersistence that was missing. Gina''s r9419h reproduced the same\nstale-states pattern in this session, and the fix now produces the\nexpected 2-key states-map after adapter restart.\n\nRefs #119.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7Wm3dJ6XTwTsJwVj19ELu","tree":{"sha":"fd71861afd2d8f3c6d5e7c48943efe93e6eaaa98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/fd71861afd2d8f3c6d5e7c48943efe93e6eaaa98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998","node_id":"C_kwDOMGdLNtoAKGM1MDczZDYxYTNlMzNkZTQyYjAzMGNmOTk3MmEwODE2MDA1NjE5OTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb","sha":"c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb"}],"sha":"c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c5073d61a3e33de42b030cf9972a081600561998"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:33:28Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:33:28Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"message":"release: v0.4.10 - Fix: axios bumped to 1.20.0 for upstream security fixes; Node.js built-in requires now use the node: prefix (lib/haDecode.js, lib/mapMerge.js)","tree":{"sha":"907d99c3cc49d162a79e2427e56cc850d07da273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/907d99c3cc49d162a79e2427e56cc850d07da273"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb","node_id":"C_kwDOMGdLNtoAKGM4MDZmYzVhMTM1OGViMzJmOGI2YTBiNzBiYjNmYzkzMmI1N2FjYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/67f605aa06c750272299552e982b6a2cc19d4e61","sha":"67f605aa06c750272299552e982b6a2cc19d4e61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/67f605aa06c750272299552e982b6a2cc19d4e61"}],"sha":"c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/c806fc5a1358eb32f8b6a0b70bb3fc932b57acbb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commits/67f605aa06c750272299552e982b6a2cc19d4e61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:23:08Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:25:53Z","email":"ds.sefina@gmail.com","name":"Sefina-DS"},"message":"chore(deps): pin typescript to ^6.0.3 — supersedes #116, see PR comment for rationale\n\nTS 7.0.2 (native Go rewrite, tsgo/Corsa) has a documented @types-resolution\nbreaking change confirmed here: go-to-point.test.js loses type-checking for\ndescribe/it, and npm run check goes from 1543 to 1856 errors (+313), including\na genuinely new lib/cleanset.js regression not present under 6.x. Pinning to\nthe last stable 6.x (6.0.3) keeps the net increase small (1543 -> 1584, +41,\nall from the pre-existing describe/it gap) without the 7.0 compiler-rewrite\nrisk. npm run check is dev-only (not part of the release/CI gate).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QYfrtd9APeCHT5jBK49oM6","tree":{"sha":"7a00b23680fe2513fdd6d26eaad3b973251210fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/trees/7a00b23680fe2513fdd6d26eaad3b973251210fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/git/commits/67f605aa06c750272299552e982b6a2cc19d4e61","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TA2k/ioBroker.dreame/commit/67f605aa06c750272299552e982b6a2cc19d4